        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "af038681-c6b5-35be-bc0e-8039b594f296",
                "word": "taptoe",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4a7cb914-05f7-4225-8c28-7d50de148673",
                        "entry_id": "af038681-c6b5-35be-bc0e-8039b594f296",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "taptoes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b71c6982-2844-3e2b-baca-7a1e7a93db5c",
                        "entry_id": "af038681-c6b5-35be-bc0e-8039b594f296",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een trompetsignaal dat oorspronkelijk werd gespeeld als afsluiting van de dag"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7cf7e13-6465-47f8-9152-3a92bfbb7471",
                                "sense_id": "b71c6982-2844-3e2b-baca-7a1e7a93db5c",
                                "text": "De taptoe werd geslagen, er werd appèl gehouden, er werd gegeten en iedereen zocht voor de nacht een plaatsje rond de vuren; de een repareerde zijn schoeisel, een ander rookte een pijpje, en weer anderen deden al hun kleren uit om er de luizen uit te stomen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f753432-6a73-44f1-8a5c-cd5d96c94592",
                                "sense_id": "b71c6982-2844-3e2b-baca-7a1e7a93db5c",
                                "text": ". Van 's morgens vroeg, dat de klapperlui naar huis gaan en de bakkers hun deur openen, tot 's avonds laat als de taptoe slaat en de herbergen sluiten, belegeren zij de straten als vliegen de boterton."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "077d2b33-d042-4c1c-b202-6070d5719a0d",
                                "sense_id": "b71c6982-2844-3e2b-baca-7a1e7a93db5c",
                                "text": "Ze oefenen voor een taptoe in augustus, een van de vele herdenkingsmomenten honderd jaar na de Derde slag bij Ieper - beter bekend als de slag om Passendale. Dit overmoedig offensief van de Britse veldmaarschalk Douglas Haig tegen de Duitse bezetter duurde van 31 juli tot 10 november 1917, legde de hele streek in puin en leverde geen duurzame terreinwinst op. Er vielen wel bijna een half miljoen slachtoffers, gewonden, zieken en krijgsgevangenen inbegrepen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c237662-f987-4bfb-919c-6a3ecf1c067f",
                                "sense_id": "b71c6982-2844-3e2b-baca-7a1e7a93db5c",
                                "text": "Bij de uitvaartceremonie die volgde, was het korps mariniers aanwezig, plus een flink aantal politieagenten en brandweermensen. En een legerhond met de naam Rex. Gedreun van saluutschoten. Het taptoe-signaal schalde."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "69e4fb28-1be1-41dd-a5f5-ad8531bdefb3",
                        "source_entry_id": "af038681-c6b5-35be-bc0e-8039b594f296",
                        "source_sense_id": "b71c6982-2844-3e2b-baca-7a1e7a93db5c",
                        "source_sense_description": "militair afsluitend signaal",
                        "target_lang_word": "tattoo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tattoo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7c537e5-3923-30e1-83b9-66d510469558",
                                        "entry_id": "53faf039-7086-37a3-97f7-9c726e960f0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An image made on a body part, usually the skin with ink and a needle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e98aee88-fb94-45c2-ac26-e1d7d8f82add",
                                                "sense_id": "b7c537e5-3923-30e1-83b9-66d510469558",
                                                "text": "His shirt sleeves were turned up, so upon his brawny arms his tattooes were visible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4d1e651-dc67-4ced-978a-b268b358cb92",
                                                "sense_id": "b7c537e5-3923-30e1-83b9-66d510469558",
                                                "text": "Nothing pleases a Burman more than to be asked to show his tattooes. He is as delighted as a collector of curios in England. They consist of a series of pictures of tigers, lions, elephants, dragons, demons, and what-not, surrounded by mottoes invoking good fortune, and round waist and knees the whole is framed by a neat floral or scroll pattern."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f68e04d-c1f1-4b87-b495-c57cce26ac87",
                                                "sense_id": "b7c537e5-3923-30e1-83b9-66d510469558",
                                                "text": "Almost a century and a half after the De Soto Expedition, Joutel (Cox, 1905, II: 139–140), one of La Salle’s men, reacted to the Caddoes in much the same way as had De la Vega, finding their tattooes particularly repulsive. The Caddoes used needles or other sharp-pointed objects to prick the skin until the blood flowed, and then rubbed powdered charcoal into the wounds. When the wounds healed, the charcoal remaining under the skin made striking tattooes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0318893-790b-4576-bbe2-63e13e9f48f8",
                                                "sense_id": "b7c537e5-3923-30e1-83b9-66d510469558",
                                                "text": "Victor was spot on, of course; in fact, I have often been tempted to seek him out when I have been plagued by diseases of the heart. He'd be able to tell me in ten seconds whether someone was worth a tattoo or not."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ffd6a26-2069-4de6-8115-abae0e55b0e0",
                                                "sense_id": "b7c537e5-3923-30e1-83b9-66d510469558",
                                                "text": "And here's a solution to an age old tattoo problem. If your girlfriend's name, say, \"Suzie,\" is tattooed on your arm, and you break up with her, don't have the tattoo removed. Just have the tattoo reworked so it says, \"Fuck Suzie.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e01debbf-cc32-3b08-8b15-d6b6133c57c2",
                                        "entry_id": "53faf039-7086-37a3-97f7-9c726e960f0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A method of decorating a body part, usually the skin, by inserting colored substances under the surface with a sharp instrument (usually a solenoid-driven needle)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tattoo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "902249fc-2d1f-3cbb-9a44-da69a57f5175",
                                        "entry_id": "a86feb86-65a9-355d-9050-3132e011611d",
